      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(cli): add exec approval recovery guidance (Fixes #53250)",
        "body": "## Summary\n\nFixes #53250.\n\nWhen `host=node` exec approval is required but no approval UI is available, the exec approval unavailable path could still fall back to generic guidance:\n\n`exec denied: approval required (approval UI not available)`\n\nThat tells the operator something is wrong, but not what to do next for a node-hosted command. This patch moves the recovery guidance into the shared exec approval unavailable renderer used by the current host=node exec path, then names two concrete recovery paths:\n- open the Control UI with `openclaw dashboard --no-open`\n- inspect pending approvals with `openclaw approvals get --node <id|name|ip>` or the resolved node id when available\n\n## Tests and validation\n\n```bash\nnode scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/infra/exec-approval-reply.test.ts src/agents/bash-tools.exec-host-shared.test.ts src/agents/embedded-agent-subscribe.handlers.tools.test.ts\ngit diff --check\n```\n\n## Real behavior proof\n\nBehavior addressed:\n- the node exec approval unavailable message should include actionable next steps instead of dead-end generic guidance\n\nEnvironment tested:\n- local source checkout on this branch\n\nEvidence after the fix:\n- `buildExecApprovalUnavailableReplyPayload({ reason: \"no-approval-route\", host: \"node\", nodeId: \"mac-1\" })` now renders both `openclaw dashboard --no-open` and `openclaw approvals get --node mac-1`\n- the host/node metadata is passed from the exec host result and preserved by the deterministic tool-result output path\n\nObserved result:\n- users hitting the current shared host=node unavailable path get concrete approval inbox commands in the message itself\n\nWhat was not tested:\n- a live node exec approval timeout/denial flow\n\n## Risk\n\nLow. This is a renderer-only guidance improvement with no behavior change in the approval flow itself.\n",
